  p10-l1  [77 74 116 87]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b}OPP-115
  p10-l2  [131 74 518 87]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b}Text:{NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i} Secure Online Ordering For your security, we only store your credit card information if
  p10-l3  [130 87 516 99]  {NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i}you choose to set up an authorized account with one of our Sites. In that case, it is stored on
  p10-l4  [131 100 516 112]  {NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i}a secure computer in an encrypted format. If you do not set up an account, you will have to
  p10-l5  [131 112 516 125]  {NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i}enter your credit card information each time you order. We understand that this may be a little
  p10-l6  [131 125 427 137]  {NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i}inconvenient for you, but some customers appreciate the added security.
  p10-l7  [131 150 478 164]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b}Classes:{Inconsolatazi4-Regular 10.3} Data Security{NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.3},{Inconsolatazi4-Regular 10.3} User Choice/Control{NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.3},{Inconsolatazi4-Regular 10.3} First Party Collection/Use
  p10-l8  [77 168 115 182]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b}APP-350
  p10-l9  [131 168 516 182]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b}Text:{NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i} Our Use of Web Beacons and Analytics Services Microsoft web pages may contain
  p10-l10  [131 182 516 194]  {NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i}electronic images known as web beacons (also called single-pixel gifs) that we use to help
  p10-l11  [131 194 516 207]  {NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i}deliver cookies on our websites, count users who have visited those websites and deliver
  p10-l12  [131 207 516 219]  {NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i}co-branded products. We also include web beacons in our promotional email messages or
  p10-l13  [131 220 378 232]  {NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i}newsletters to determine whether you open and act on them.
  p10-l14  [131 245 458 259]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b}Classes:{Inconsolatazi4-Regular 10.3} Contact_E_Mail_Address{NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.3},{Inconsolatazi4-Regular 10.3} Identifier_Cookie_or_similar_Tech
  p10-l15  [77 263 516 277]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b}PrivacyQA Sentence:{NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i} We may collect and use information about your location (such as your country) or
  p10-l16  [131 276 516 289]  {NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i}infer your approximate location based on your IP address in order to provide you with tailored
  p10-l17  [131 289 516 301]  {NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i}educational experiences for your region, but we don’t collect the precise geolocation of you or
  p10-l18  [130 302 181 314]  {NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i}your device.
  p10-l19  [131 327 395 341]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b}Question:{NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i} Does the app track my location?{NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b} Answer:{Inconsolatazi4-Regular 10.3} Relevant
  p10-l20  [77 345 119 359]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b}PolicyQA
  p10-l21  [131 345 516 359]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b}Text:{NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i} Illini Media never shares personally identifiable information provided to us online in
  p10-l22  [131 358 516 371]  {NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i}ways unrelated to the ones described above without allowing you to opt out or otherwise
  p10-l23  [130 371 516 383]  {NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i}prohibit such unrelated uses. Google or any ad server may use information (not including your
  p10-l24  [131 384 516 396]  {NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i}name, address, email address, or telephone number) about your visits to this and other websites
  p10-l25  [131 397 454 409]  {NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i}in order to provide advertisements about goods and services of interest to you.
  p10-l26  [131 422 452 435]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b}Question:{NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.3} Do you share my data with others? If yes, what is the type of data?
  p10-l27  [131 435 516 448]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b}Answer:{NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i} information (not including your name, address, email address or telephone number)
  p10-l28  [77 453 114 466]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b}PolicyIE
  p10-l29  [131 453 516 466]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b}Sentence:{NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i} We may also use or display your username and icon or profile photo for marketing
  p10-l30  [130 466 242 478]  {NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i}purposes or press releases.
  p10-l31  [131 491 276 504]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b}Intent:{Inconsolatazi4-Regular 10.3} Data Collection/Usage
  p10-l32  [289 491 517 504]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b}Slots:{NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.3} (1){NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i} Data Collector: First Party Entity–We{NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.3}, (2)
  p10-l33  [130 504 518 517]  {NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i}Action–use{NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.3}, (3){NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i} Data Provider: User–your{NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.3}, (4){NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i} Data Collected: User Online Activities/Profiles–
  p10-l34  [131 517 517 529]  {NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i}username{NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.3}, (5){NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i} Data Collected: User Online Activities/Profiles–icon or profile photo{NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.3}, (6)
  p10-l35  [130 530 421 542]  {NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i}Purpose: Advertising/Marketing–marketing purpose or press releases{NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.3}.
  p10-l36  [77 547 91 561]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b}PI-
  p10-l37  [77 560 110 574]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b}Extract
  p10-l38  [131 547 516 561]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b}Text:{NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i} We may share aggregate demographic and usage information with our prospective and
  p10-l39  [131 561 488 573]  {NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i}actual business partners, advertisers, and other third parties for any business purpose.
  p10-l40  [131 586 400 599]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.3 b}Entities:{Inconsolatazi4-Regular 10.3} SHARE{NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.3} –{NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal 10.3 i} aggregate demographic and usage information
  p10-l41  [211 607 384 619]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10}Table 4: Examples from the tasks in PLUE.
  p10-l42  [71 635 289 648]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}and uses more training data to achieve remarkable
  p10-l43  [71 648 291 661]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}performance improvements. Note that while BERT,
  p10-l44  [71 662 290 675]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}Electra, and SpanBERT use the same vocabulary,
  p10-l45  [71 675 289 688]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}RoBERTa uses a different vocabulary resulting in
  p10-l46  [70 689 226 702]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}15M more parameters in the model.
  p10-l47  [71 706 143 721]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.9 b}LEGAL-BERT
  p10-l48  [154 707 291 720]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}Chalkidis et al. (2020) pre-
  p10-l49  [71 720 289 733]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}trained BERT using 12 GB of the English text
  p10-l50  [70 734 289 747]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}(over 351K documents) from several legal fields
  p10-l51  [70 747 289 761]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}(e.g., contracts, legislation, court cases) scraped
  p10-l52  [71 761 290 774]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}from publicly available resources. Since privacy
  p10-l53  [306 635 524 648]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}policies serve as official documents to protect the
  p10-l54  [306 648 524 661]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}company and consumers’ privacy rights and might
  p10-l55  [306 662 526 675]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}contain contents in response to privacy law (e.g.,
  p10-l56  [306 675 524 688]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}GDPR), we study LEGAL-BERT’s effectiveness
  p10-l57  [306 689 390 702]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}on the PLUE tasks.
