  p11-l1  [71 70 242 86]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 12 b}D More Implementation Details
  p11-l2  [71 93 87 108]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.9 b}D.1
  p11-l3  [98 93 282 108]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.9 b}Domain-specific Continual Pre-training
  p11-l4  [71 111 289 124]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}Since BERT, Electra, and SpanBERT share the
  p11-l5  [71 125 289 138]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}same model architectures, we use almost the same
  p11-l6  [71 138 290 151]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}hyperparameters (e.g., learning rate, train steps,
  p11-l7  [71 152 291 165]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}batch size) for them following the original papers.
  p11-l8  [70 165 290 179]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}We scale down the train steps by the same factor,
  p11-l9  [71 179 290 192]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}as the size of our pre-training corpus is roughly
  p11-l10  [70 193 291 206]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}1/10 the size of the pre-training corpus of BERT.
  p11-l11  [70 206 291 219]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}We adhere to the guidelines outlined in Liu et al.
  p11-l12  [70 220 290 233]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}(2019) to train RoBERTa with larger batch size,
  p11-l13  [71 233 289 246]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}higher learning rate, and fewer train steps. Table 5
  p11-l14  [71 247 282 260]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}presents the training hyperparameters for PLMs.
  p11-l15  [71 269 87 283]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.9 b}D.2
  p11-l16  [98 269 215 283]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.9 b}Task-specific Fine-tuning
  p11-l17  [70 287 289 300]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}We fine-tune the models for each task using the
  p11-l18  [70 300 289 313]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}Adam (Kingma and Ba, 2015) optimizer with a
  p11-l19  [71 314 289 327]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}batch size of 32. We fine-tune the models on the
  p11-l20  [71 327 289 340]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}QA tasks for 3 epochs and other tasks for 20 epochs
  p11-l21  [71 341 289 354]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}and perform a grid search on the learning rate for
  p11-l22  [71 354 289 367]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}each task with validation examples. We chose the
  p11-l23  [71 368 289 381]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}learning rate for tasks without validation examples
  p11-l24  [71 381 289 395]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}based on our findings from the tasks with validation
  p11-l25  [71 395 289 408]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}examples. Table 6 lists the hyperparameters for all
  p11-l26  [71 409 167 422]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}the downstream tasks.
  p11-l27  [82 422 289 435]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}In OPP-115 and APP-350, we compute the class
  p11-l28  [70 436 291 449]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}weights (the class weights are inversely propor-
  p11-l29  [71 449 290 462]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}tional to the occurrences of the classes) and apply
  p11-l30  [71 463 289 476]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}them in fine-tuning, as we find out both datasets
  p11-l31  [71 476 289 489]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}have the class-imbalance problem and using class
  p11-l32  [70 490 289 503]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}weights brings gains to overall performance. We
  p11-l33  [71 503 290 517]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}also report the human performances for PrivacyQA
  p11-l34  [71 517 236 530]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}and PolicyIE from the original works.
  p11-l35  [71 539 87 553]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.9 b}D.3
  p11-l36  [98 539 166 553]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 10.9 b}Software Tools
  p11-l37  [71 557 291 570]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}To facilitate using PLUE, we release our implemen-
  p11-l38  [71 570 290 584]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}tation, which is built with Pytorch (Paszke et al.,
  p11-l39  [71 583 291 597]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}2019) and the Huggingface transformers{NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 8}5{NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9} pack-
  p11-l40  [71 597 289 611]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}age. Our implementation includes the continual
  p11-l41  [71 611 289 624]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}pre-training of our baselines and the evaluation
  p11-l42  [71 625 291 638]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}of any PLMs supported by the Huggingface trans-
  p11-l43  [71 638 291 651]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}formers package on the PLUE benchmark tasks.
  p11-l44  [71 652 291 665]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}In addition to PLUE datasets, we release the pre-
  p11-l45  [71 665 291 678]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}training corpus and all data pre-processing scripts,
  p11-l46  [71 679 290 692]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}including the pre-training corpus crawling scripts,
  p11-l47  [71 692 227 705]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}to assist future research in this area.
  p11-l48  [84 762 280 773]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 6}5{Inconsolatazi4-Regular 9} https://github.com/huggingface/transformers
  p11-l49  [291 781 307 794]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}362
