  p3-l96  [335 317 496 329]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10}Table 2: Structures for Negative Answer
  p3-l97  [306 351 524 364]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}Curie-001, Babbage-001, and Ada-001. According
  p3-l98  [306 364 524 377]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}to the GPT-3 documentation, Davinci-003 is the
  p3-l99  [306 378 503 391]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}most powerful model and Ada-001, the least.
  p3-l100  [306 400 361 415]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 12 b}5 Results
  p3-l101  [306 422 526 435]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}Figure 1 gives the accuracy for ellipsis and non-
  p3-l102  [306 436 524 449]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}ellipsis, for each of the five models. We have set
  p3-l103  [306 449 524 462]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}up the test examples so that an ellipsis example
  p3-l104  [306 463 526 476]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}is paired with a non-ellipsis example that is oth-
  p3-l105  [306 476 524 490]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}erwise identical. Because of this, we claim that
  p3-l106  [306 490 524 503]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}the difference in accuracy of the non-ellipsis case
  p3-l107  [306 504 524 517]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}vs. the ellipsis case provides a measurement of the
  p3-l108  [306 517 524 530]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}difficulty specifically posed by ellipsis. For all but
  p3-l109  [306 531 526 544]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}the least powerful model, Ada, the non-ellipsis ac-
  p3-l110  [306 544 526 557]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}curacy is substantially higher than ellipsis accuracy,
  p3-l111  [306 558 524 571]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}supporting the hypothesis that ellipsis-dependent
  p3-l112  [306 571 524 584]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}reasoning presents a difficult challenge for these
  p3-l113  [306 585 524 598]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}models. While the Ada model actually performs
  p3-l114  [306 598 524 612]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}somewhat better for ellipsis than non-ellipsis, this
  p3-l115  [306 612 526 625]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}is not because the Ada model does well with ellip-
  p3-l116  [306 625 524 639]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}sis cases; rather, the model has great difficulty with
  p3-l117  [306 639 524 652]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}both the ellipsis and non-ellipsis cases, and is close
  p3-l118  [306 653 469 666]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}to a random guessing baseline of .50.
  p3-l119  [317 666 524 679]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}In figures 2 through 6, we present results for each
  p3-l120  [306 680 526 693]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}model. We show the accuracy for each structure,
  p3-l121  [306 693 526 706]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}for both the ellipsis version and the non-ellipsis ver-
  p3-l122  [306 707 526 720]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}sion. Consider the most powerful models, Davinci-
  p3-l123  [306 720 524 733]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}003 and Davinci-002. In figures 2 and 3, we can see
  p3-l124  [306 734 526 747]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}that ellipsis is not difficult in the first two structures:
  p3-l125  [306 747 524 761]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}2Sent (Separate Sentence) and 1Sent (Conjoined
  p3-l126  [306 761 525 774]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}Sentence). Here the accuracy is nearly perfect for
