  p4-l10  [71 575 289 588]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}lipsis is quite challenging, with accuracies ranging
  p4-l11  [71 588 291 601]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}from 48.8 to 85.8. The Backwards and Two Ac-
  p4-l12  [71 602 290 615]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}tions structures are even more difficult for ellipsis.
  p4-l13  [71 627 132 643]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 12 b}6 Analysis
  p4-l14  [71 652 289 665]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}For the two most powerful models, it is clear that
  p4-l15  [71 665 289 678]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}ellipsis poses a difficult challenge, except in the two
  p4-l16  [71 679 289 692]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}simplest ellipsis structures. For the less powerful
  p4-l17  [71 692 290 705]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}models, the picture is mixed. For these models,
  p4-l18  [71 706 289 719]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}the non-ellipsis examples are themselves a difficult
  p4-l19  [71 719 289 733]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}challenge, so we are not able to observe the specific
  p4-l20  [71 733 195 746]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}difficulties posed by ellipsis.
  p4-l21  [82 747 289 761]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}As we can see in figure 1, the Davinci-002 model
  p4-l22  [71 761 291 774]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}performs somewhat better overall than Davinci-
  p4-l23  [306 246 526 258]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10}Figure 3: Ellipsis Accuracy – davinci-002 (1000 exam-
  p4-l24  [306 258 381 270]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10}ples per structure.)
  p4-l25  [306 459 524 471]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10}Figure 4: Ellipsis Accuracy – curie-001 (1000 examples
  p4-l26  [306 471 362 483]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10}per structure.)
  p4-l27  [306 507 526 520]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}003, on both ellipsis and non-ellipsis. However,
  p4-l28  [306 520 526 533]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}figures 2 and 3 show that the advantage of Davinci-
  p4-l29  [306 534 526 547]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}002 on ellipsis is exclusively due to the subordi-
  p4-l30  [306 547 526 561]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}nate antecedent construction. In every other el-
  p4-l31  [306 561 524 574]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}lipsis structure, Davinci-003 performs better than
  p4-l32  [306 575 363 588]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}Davinci-002.
  p4-l33  [317 589 524 602]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}There are striking differences in the distribution
  p4-l34  [306 603 526 616]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}of errors. For both the Davinci-003 and Davinci-
  p4-l35  [306 616 524 629]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}002 models, errors are nearly always false negatives
  p4-l36  [305 630 525 643]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}– that is, incorrect “No" answers. There are virtually
  p4-l37  [306 643 526 656]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}no false positives, either for the ellipsis case or non-
  p4-l38  [306 657 524 670]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}ellipsis case. For the other three models, there are
  p4-l39  [306 670 524 683]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}many errors of each type, with a much higher ratio
  p4-l40  [306 684 382 697]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}of false positives.
  p4-l41  [306 709 381 725]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 12 b}7 Conclusion
  p4-l42  [306 734 524 747]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}Most of the current rapid progress in NLP is due
  p4-l43  [306 747 524 761]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}to pre-trained large language models. GPT-3 is
  p4-l44  [306 761 524 774]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}an impressive publicly available collection of such
  p4-l45  [293 781 304 794]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}42
