  p5-l115  [516 403 524 411]  {MSAM10 10.9}■
  p5-l116  [306 426 467 437]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 12 b}5 Generalization to Semirings
  p5-l117  [306 448 526 458]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}It turns out that Jelinek–Lafferty, and, by extension,
  p5-l118  [306 461 524 471]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}our improved algorithm, can be generalized to
  p5-l119  [306 475 524 485]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}work for semiring-weighted CFGs, with the same
  p5-l120  [306 489 524 498]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}time complexity, under the condition that the
  p5-l121  [306 502 524 512]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}semiring is closed, i.e., it has a Kleene star. This
  p5-l122  [306 516 524 526]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}follows from the fact that the only operations used
  p5-l123  [306 529 524 539]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}by the algorithm are addition and multiplication
  p5-l124  [306 543 524 553]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}if we use Lehmann’s (1977) algorithm for the
  p5-l125  [306 556 524 566]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}computation of left-corner expectations,{CMMI10 10.9 i} ξ{NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}. We
  p5-l126  [306 570 524 580]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}can even relax the condition of local normalization
  p5-l127  [306 583 524 593]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}by changing how left-corner expectations and the
  p5-l128  [306 597 524 607]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}weight of the prefix{CMMI10 10.9 i} ε{NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9} are computed. The relevant
  p5-l129  [306 611 524 620]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}definitions and derivation of the adapted algorithm
  p5-l130  [306 624 411 634]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}can be found in App. B.
  p5-l131  [306 647 381 658]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 12 b}6 Conclusion
  p5-l132  [306 669 525 679]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}In this paper, we have shown how to efficiently
  p5-l133  [306 682 526 692]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}compute prefix probabilities for PCFGs in CNF,
  p5-l134  [306 696 526 706]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}adapting Jelinek–Lafferty to use additional memo-
  p5-l135  [306 709 524 719]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}ization, thereby reducing the time complexity from
  p5-l136  [306 721 526 733]  {CMSY10 10.9 i}O{CMR10 10.9}({CMMI10 10.9 i}N{CMR8 8}3{CMSY10 10.9 i} |N |{CMR8 8}3{CMR10 10.9} +{CMSY10 10.9 i} |N |{CMR8 8}4{CMR10 10.9} ){NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9} to{CMSY10 10.9 i} O{CMR10 10.9}({CMMI10 10.9 i}N{CMR8 8}2{CMSY10 10.9 i} |N |{CMR8 8}3{CMR10 10.9} +{CMMI10 10.9 i} N{CMR8 8}3{CMSY10 10.9 i} |N |{CMR8 8}2{CMR10 10.9} ){NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}.
  p5-l137  [306 736 524 746]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}We thereby addressed one of the main limitations
  p5-l138  [306 750 524 760]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}of the original formulation, of being slow for large
  p5-l139  [306 764 372 773]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}grammar sizes.
  p5-l140  [292 783 303 793]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}61
  == page 6  595 x 842  lines 104  pictures 0  drawings 0
  p6-l1  [71 74 130 84]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 12 b}Limitations
  p6-l2  [70 95 289 104]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}While we have improved the asymptotic running
  p6-l3  [71 108 289 118]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}time of a classic algorithm with regard to grammar
  p6-l4  [71 122 289 132]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}size, the time complexity of our algorithm is still
  p6-l5  [71 135 289 145]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}cubic in the length of the input. Our result follows
  p6-l6  [71 149 289 159]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}the tradition of dynamic programming algorithms
  p6-l7  [71 162 289 172]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}that trade time for space by memoizing and reusing
  p6-l8  [71 176 289 186]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}precomputed intermediate results. The usefulness
  p6-l9  [71 189 289 199]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}of this trade-off in practice depends on the specifics
  p6-l10  [71 203 290 213]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}of the grammar, and while the complexity is strictly
  p6-l11  [71 217 289 226]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}better in terms of non-terminals, it will be most
  p6-l12  [71 230 291 240]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}noticeable for denser grammars with many non-
  p6-l13  [71 244 114 253]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}terminals.
  p6-l14  [71 266 158 277]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Medi 12 b}Ethics Statement
  p6-l15  [70 287 289 297]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}We do not foresee any ethical issues arising from
  p6-l16  [71 301 114 310]  {NimbusRomNo9L-Regu 10.9}this work.
