  p3-l150  [327 520 562 529]  {CMTI10 10 i}Experimental observation{CMR10 10}. In systems with topological
  p3-l151  [317 531 562 540]  {CMR10 10}textures disorder yields contributions formally of zeroth
  p3-l152  [317 543 562 552]  {CMR10 10}order in the disorder strength, which are hard to distin-
  p3-l153  [317 554 562 563]  {CMR10 10}guish experimentally from the intrinsic terms in the DC
  p3-l154  [317 566 562 575]  {CMR10 10}regime. However, it should be possible to distinguish the
  p3-l155  [317 577 562 586]  {CMR10 10}intrinsic and extrinsic contributions to the OHE using
  p3-l156  [317 588 562 597]  {CMR10 10}AC techniques. This would be the orbital transport ana-
  p3-l157  [317 600 562 609]  {CMR10 10}logue of the magneto-optical Kerr effect [70], which was
  p3-l158  [317 611 562 620]  {CMR10 10}shown to be a strong probe of intrinsic transport in the
  p3-l159  [317 623 562 632]  {CMR10 10}anomalous Hall effect of topological insulators. Since dis-
  p3-l160  [317 634 562 644]  {CMR10 10}order effects are suppressed as 1{CMMI10 10 i}/{CMR10 10}({CMMI10 10 i}ωτ{CMR10 10} ), with{CMMI10 10 i} ω{CMR10 10} the light
  p3-l161  [317 645 562 655]  {CMR10 10}frequency, one requires{CMMI10 10 i} ωτ{CMSY10 10 i} ≫{CMR10 10} 1. Taking{CMMI10 10 i} τ{CMSY10 10 i} ∼{CMR10 10} 0{CMMI10 10 i}.{CMR10 10}1ps places
  p3-l162  [317 657 489 666]  {CMR10 10}the wavelength in the ultraviolet range.
