  p6-l2  [72 56 299 64]  {CMR9 9}the same. This behaviour is also present in the Berry
  p6-l3  [72 66 299 75]  {CMR9 9}curvature, as discussed in Ref. [81] for anomalous Hall
  p6-l4  [72 76 299 85]  {CMR9 9}effect. In this paper, if we take the ∆{CMSY9 9 i} →{CMR9 9} 0 at the very
  p6-l5  [72 87 299 95]  {CMR9 9}beginning of graphene Hamiltonian, the OHE disappears
  p6-l6  [72 97 299 106]  {CMR9 9}altogether. But if we take the ∆{CMSY9 9 i} →{CMR9 9} 0 limit for the orbital
  p6-l7  [72 106 299 117]  {CMR9 9}moment, it yields lim{CMR6 6}∆{CMSY6 6 i}→{CMR6 6}0{CMR9 9}∆{CMMI9 9 i}/{CMR9 9}({CMMI9 9 i}q{CMR6 6} 2{CMMI9 9 i} v{CMR6 6} 2{CMMI6 6 i} F{CMR9 9} + ∆{CMR6 6}2{CMR9 9} ) ={CMMI9 9 i} πδ{CMR9 9}({CMMI9 9 i}q{CMR6 6} 2{CMMI9 9 i} v{CMR6 6} 2{CMMI6 6 i} F{CMR9 9} ).
  p6-l8  [72 119 299 127]  {CMR9 9}For the intrinsic case, the Fermi energy lies exactly at the
  p6-l9  [72 129 299 137]  {CMR9 9}Dirac point. The ∆{CMSY9 9 i} →{CMR9 9} 0 limit will make the intrinsic OH-
  p6-l10  [72 139 299 148]  {CMR9 9}conductance diverge after performing the integral over
  p6-l11  [72 149 299 158]  {CMR9 9}the Fermi sea [33]. Hence, formally, the intrinsic OH-
  p6-l12  [72 160 299 169]  {CMR9 9}conductance will diverge when the{CMMI9 9 i} E{CMMI6 6 i}F{CMR9 9} is in band gap and
  p6-l13  [72 171 299 179]  {CMR9 9}the extrinsic OH-conductance will vanish for graphene.
  p6-l14  [72 181 299 189]  {CMR9 9}However, in realistic samples, we expect that once the
  p6-l15  [72 192 299 200]  {CMR9 9}gap reaches below a certain value it will be overwhelmed
  p6-l16  [72 202 299 210]  {CMR9 9}by disorder and such a divergence will not be observable
  p6-l17  [72 213 299 221]  {CMR9 9}in practice. The limit of vanishing gap makes sense only
  p6-l18  [72 223 299 231]  {CMR9 9}for graphene which is a gapless material in a pristine
  p6-l19  [72 233 299 242]  {CMR9 9}situation. The ∆{CMSY9 9 i} →{CMR9 9} 0 limit is not applicable to TMDs,
  p6-l20  [72 244 299 252]  {CMR9 9}since the band gap of monolayer TMDs is inherent to the
  p6-l21  [72 254 202 263]  {CMR9 9}band structure of materials [45].
